:"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If more than one spell says that lands you control don’t untap during your next untap step, the effects will all wear off during that untap step. You’ll untap lands you control during your untap step after that one.","oracle_id":"c010d833-1873-4132-b4ff-8d78b3d7c2d7","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"No lands that you control will untap during your next untap step, even lands that aren’t tapped as this spell resolves. This includes lands that enter the battlefield after this spell resolves.","oracle_id":"c010d833-1873-4132-b4ff-8d78b3d7c2d7","published_at":"2017-07-14","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If multiple \"extra turn\" effects resolve in the same turn, take them in the reverse of the order that the effects resolved. In other words, the most recently created extra turn is taken first.","oracle_id":"dbd6a94b-62ff-4a10-9d52-bdd90b26e425","published_at":"2022-12-08","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
